2026-09-01 14:47:59 [DEBUG] [visit_node] matched_context (rag_context) (len=1718)="\n\nName: CBC\nDescription: The Complete Blood Count (CBC) quantifies the concentration of red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets within the circulatory system. It is used to evaluate overall health, detect infections, identify anemia, and monitor various hematological disorders or blood cancers. This panel provides critical data regarding the oxygen-carrying capacity of blood and the integrity of the immune system's cellular response.\nPrice: 160.0\nSample Type: Blood\nDuration: في نفس اليوم\nPatient Instructions: لا يوجد تحضير خاص لهذا التحليل.\n\nName: WBCs.Total & Differential\nDescription: This test measures the total count of white blood cells and the specific proportions of different leukocyte types, including neutrophils, lymphocytes, monocytes, eosinophils, and basophils. It is used to evaluate the immune system's response to infection, inflammation, stress, or bone marrow disorders. Clinicians order this panel to assist in diagnosing conditions such as leukemia, systemic infections, allergies, and autoimmune diseases.\nPrice: 80.0\nSample Type: Blood\nDuration: نفس اليوم\nPatient Instructions: لا يوجد تحضير خاص لهذا التحليل.\n\nName: Platelets count\nDescription: The Platelets count measures the number of thrombocytes circulating in the blood, which are essential for blood clotting and wound healing. It is ordered to evaluate unexplained bruising, excessive bleeding, or to monitor patients undergoing chemotherapy or those with bone marrow disorders. This assessment is critical for diagnosing conditions such as thrombocytopenia, thrombocytosis, and various hematological malignancies.\nPrice: 80.0\nSample Type: Blood\nDuration: نفس اليوم\nPatient Instructions: لا يوجد تحضير خاص لهذا التحليل."
